## Context

Task 6 in multi-branch trail support. The trail store currently uses unconditional `SetReference` which can silently clobber concurrent writes. With multi-branch trails, two worktrees working on different branches of the same trail could race on checkpoint appends. `CheckAndSetReference` provides compare-and-swap semantics — the write fails if the ref moved since we read it, and we retry.

go-git v6 provides:
- `repo.Storer.CheckAndSetReference(newRef, oldRef)` — atomic CAS
- `storage.ErrReferenceHasChanged` — error when CAS fails (from `github.com/go-git/go-git/v6/storage`)

